---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'What does technical SEO involve for Birmingham businesses?',
    a: 'Technical SEO fixes the infrastructure that decides whether search engines can crawl, index, and rank your site. Broken foundations mean lost rankings. We sort that out for Birmingham businesses across manufacturing, professional services, and retail.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How long does a technical SEO audit take?',
    a: 'Five to ten working days. A 20-page brochure site is faster. A large e-commerce platform with thousands of product pages takes longer. We scope it on the call.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does technical SEO cost in Birmingham?',
    a: 'Audits start at £500. Ongoing technical retainers for Birmingham organisations run £500 to £2,000 per month, depending on site complexity and how much needs fixing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does technical SEO affect AI search visibility?',
    a: 'Yes. Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, and Perplexity all depend on well-structured, fast pages with clean markup. If your site is not machine-readable, AI will not cite it.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are Core Web Vitals and why do they matter?',
    a: 'Core Web Vitals are Google\'s page experience benchmarks. LCP measures loading speed. INP measures responsiveness. CLS measures visual stability. They are a confirmed ranking factor. Fail them and your Birmingham competitors overtake you.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do WordPress sites need technical SEO?',
    a: 'Almost always. Bloated plugins kill page speed. Tag and category archives create duplicate content. Mobile rendering breaks. Structured data is missing. We find and fix every one of these problems.',
  },
];

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Technical SEO Birmingham',
  description: 'Technical SEO services for Birmingham businesses including site audits, Core Web Vitals optimisation, crawlability fixes, and structured data implementation.',
  provider: {
    '@type': 'Organization',
    name: 'SEO Birmingham',
    url: 'https://seo-birmingham.uk',
    sameAs: [],
    areaServed: {
      '@type': 'City',
      name: 'Birmingham',
      containedInPlace: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'West Midlands' },
    },
  },
  serviceType: 'Technical SEO',
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'City',
    name: 'Birmingham',
    containedInPlace: { '@type': 'AdministrativeArea', name: 'West Midlands' },
  },
  offers: {
    '@type': 'Offer',
    price: '500',
    priceCurrency: 'GBP',
    priceSpecification: {
      '@type': 'UnitPriceSpecification',
      price: '500',
      priceCurrency: 'GBP',
      unitText: 'per audit',
      description: 'Starting from £500 per technical SEO audit',
    },
  },
};

const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---

<Base
  title="Technical SEO Birmingham | SEO Birmingham"
  description="Technical SEO for Birmingham businesses. Site speed, Core Web Vitals, crawlability, structured data, and mobile-first audits from £500. We find the problems. We fix them."
  schema={[serviceSchema, faqSchema]}
  ogType="website"
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose">
    <h1>Technical SEO Birmingham</h1>

    <p>Your site is slow. We fix that. Your pages are not indexed. We fix that too. Technical SEO is the foundation everything else sits on. Without it, your content and backlinks count for nothing. We deliver systematic technical SEO for Birmingham businesses across Google, Bing, and AI search platforms.</p>

    <div class="quick-answer">
      <strong>Quick Answer:</strong> Technical SEO removes the invisible barriers that stop search engines indexing your site. For Birmingham businesses, that means faster pages, clean architecture, validated structured data, and mobile-first design that turns local searchers into customers. Audits start from <a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">£500</a>. <a href="/free-seo-audit-birmingham/">Get the audit</a>.
    </div>

    <section>
      <h2>What Technical SEO Does for Birmingham Businesses</h2>

      <p>Technical SEO deals with infrastructure. Server response times. Crawl efficiency. Indexation control. Structured data integrity. Security protocols. Get these right and search engines process your site without friction. Get them wrong and you lose ground to competitors who did not.</p>

      <p>Birmingham is one of the most competitive commercial markets outside London. Whether you operate from the Colmore Business District, trade from the <a href="/areas/">Jewellery Quarter</a>, or serve event clients near the NEC, your website competes against hundreds of local rivals for the same search queries. Technical SEO stops you losing that competition on infrastructure alone.</p>

      <p>We see the same problems on Birmingham business websites every week. Slow server response times from budget hosting. Orphaned pages invisible to crawlers. Duplicate content across product variants. Missing or broken structured data. Each one costs you rankings and revenue.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Core Web Vitals Optimisation</h2>

      <p>Core Web Vitals are Google's page experience benchmarks. They affect rankings directly. They shape how users perceive your site in the first seconds of loading. Fail them and you pay the price.</p>

      <h3>Largest Contentful Paint (LCP)</h3>
      <p>LCP measures how quickly your main content becomes visible. Google wants this under 2.5 seconds. Corporate websites in the Colmore Business District routinely fail LCP because of unoptimised hero images and render-blocking scripts from legacy CMS platforms. Custard Factory startups on modern frameworks do better but still hit delays from third-party widget loading. We strip the bloat and hit the target.</p>

      <h3>Interaction to Next Paint (INP)</h3>
      <p>INP measures how fast your site responds when someone clicks, taps, or presses a key. E-commerce sites serving Birmingham's Bullring and Grand Central struggle here. Heavy JavaScript from product filtering, live stock checkers, and payment integrations drags response times down. We cut what is not needed and optimise what is.</p>

      <h3>Cumulative Layout Shift (CLS)</h3>
      <p>CLS tracks unexpected visual movement during page load. Elements shift. Users click the wrong thing. They leave. This is particularly damaging for service businesses where layout instability kills conversions before you even get a chance.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Crawlability and Indexation</h2>

      <p>If search engines cannot crawl your site efficiently, your pages will not appear in results. Full stop. Content quality is irrelevant if Google never sees it. Crawlability issues are among the most frequent problems we diagnose in <a href="/seo-audit-birmingham/">Birmingham SEO audits</a>.</p>

      <h3>Common Crawl Issues in Birmingham E-Commerce</h3>
      <p>Birmingham has a thriving retail and e-commerce sector. Independent Jewellery Quarter retailers selling online. Bullring brands expanding into direct-to-consumer channels. These sites suffer from predictable problems:</p>

      <ul>
        <li>Faceted navigation generating thousands of duplicate URLs that waste crawl budget</li>
        <li>Session IDs appended to URLs, creating infinite crawl loops</li>
        <li>Orphaned product pages from discontinued stock still sitting in the index</li>
        <li>Pagination without proper rel=next/prev or canonical signals</li>
        <li>Broken internal links from site redesigns or platform migrations</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Indexation Control</h3>
      <p>Not every page deserves to be indexed. Admin pages, staging environments, thin filter pages, internal search results — they all dilute your quality signals. We implement precise indexation controls using robots.txt directives, meta robots tags, and canonical URLs. Google indexes only the pages that deserve to rank. Nothing else.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Structured Data and Schema Markup</h2>

      <p>Structured data tells search engines exactly what your content represents. Correct schema markup triggers rich results. Rich results increase click-through rates. Higher click-through rates mean more traffic from the same rankings.</p>

      <h3>Essential Schema Types for Birmingham Companies</h3>

      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Schema Type</th>
            <th>Best For</th>
            <th>Rich Result</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>LocalBusiness</td>
            <td>Any Birmingham business with a physical location</td>
            <td>Knowledge panel, local pack</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Product</td>
            <td>Jewellery Quarter retailers, Bullring e-commerce</td>
            <td>Price, availability, reviews in SERPs</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Service</td>
            <td>Professional services, Colmore consultancies</td>
            <td>Service details in knowledge panel</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>FAQPage</td>
            <td>Any page with frequently asked questions</td>
            <td>Expandable FAQ in search results</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Event</td>
            <td>NEC exhibitions, Digbeth venue operators</td>
            <td>Event listings with dates and tickets</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <p>We implement all structured data as JSON-LD inline on each page, following Google's current specifications. Every schema block is validated against Schema.org before deployment. No shortcuts.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Site Architecture for Multi-Location Businesses</h2>

      <p>Multiple locations need architecture that works for both users and search engines. A solicitor with offices on Colmore Row, in Solihull, and in Sutton Coldfield needs dedicated location pages with unique content. Not templated copies with the town name swapped out.</p>

      <p>Effective multi-location architecture means a clear URL hierarchy (/areas/solihull/, /areas/sutton-coldfield/), internal linking between location pages and <a href="/services/">service pages</a>, and locally relevant content that proves genuine presence in each area. This structure also supports <a href="/ai-search-optimisation-birmingham/">AI search optimisation</a> by giving machine learning models clear geographic context.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Mobile-First Indexing for Local Search</h2>

      <p>Google uses mobile-first indexing. It crawls and ranks the mobile version of your site. For Birmingham local search, this matters because most "near me" queries come from mobile devices used by people physically in the city.</p>

      <p>Someone on New Street searching "solicitor near me" expects your site to load instantly, show a phone number prominently, and display a Birmingham address clearly. If your mobile site loads slowly, presents tiny tap targets, or buries contact information behind navigation layers, that potential client goes to a competitor. Every time.</p>

      <p>We test every client site on real devices. Not just Chrome DevTools emulation. Real-world performance on mid-range Android devices over 4G connections is the benchmark that matters for Birmingham local searchers.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>HTTPS and Security Protocols</h2>

      <p>HTTPS is a baseline ranking signal. Every page must load over a valid SSL/TLS certificate with no mixed content warnings. Beyond rankings, HTTPS protects customer data and builds trust. That matters for e-commerce sites and service businesses handling enquiry forms or payment details.</p>

      <p>Common security problems we find: expired certificates, mixed content from legacy HTTP image URLs, insecure form submissions, and missing security headers like Content-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options. All fixable. All worth fixing.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>International SEO for Birmingham Manufacturers</h2>

      <p>Birmingham has a substantial export-oriented manufacturing sector. Precision engineering in Aston. Automotive components across the wider West Midlands. If you sell internationally, your technical SEO needs to handle multiple languages and regional targeting correctly.</p>

      <p>That means hreflang implementation to signal language and regional variants to Google, country-specific domain or subdirectory strategies, currency and unit localisation, and server-side content negotiation. Get hreflang wrong and the German version of your product page outranks the English version for UK searchers. We make sure that does not happen.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Technical SEO and AI Search Visibility</h2>

      <p>AI search platforms crawl and cite well-structured websites. Google AI Overviews, ChatGPT, Perplexity — they all favour the same foundations that traditional search engines reward.</p>

      <p>Clean HTML semantics. Comprehensive schema markup. Fast page speeds. Logical site architecture. These are what make your site visible to AI. Sites with poor technical health get crawled less by AI training pipelines and cited less in AI-generated responses. Our <a href="/ai-search-optimisation-birmingham/">AI search optimisation</a> page covers this in detail.</p>
    </section>

    <div class="cta-box">
      <h2 style="color: white; margin-top: 0;">Get the Audit</h2>
      <p>Find out exactly what is holding your site back. Speed. Crawlability. Structured data. Mobile experience. Security. We cover it all.</p>
      <a href="/free-seo-audit-birmingham/">Get the audit</a>
    </div>

    <section class="faq-section">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{faq.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{faq.a}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Related Services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/">SEO Birmingham</a> — full SEO services overview</li>
        <li><a href="/services/">All SEO Services</a></li>
        <li><a href="/seo-audit-birmingham/">SEO Audit Birmingham</a> — comprehensive site audit</li>
        <li><a href="/ai-search-optimisation-birmingham/">AI Search Optimisation Birmingham</a></li>
        <li><a href="/industries/">Industry-Specific SEO</a></li>
        <li><a href="/seo-pricing-birmingham/">SEO Pricing</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
